Privacy Policy
Effective Date: September 20, 2026

Last Updated: September 20, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Asfysh ("we," "our," or "us") collects, uses, and safeguards information when you interact with our website, software, APIs, and associated services (collectively, the "Service").

By connecting your Google Account or using Asfysh, you agree to the practices described in this policy.

1. Information We Process
A. Authentication Credentials & Tokens
To adapt Google Drive endpoints for Rclone, Asfysh requests access via Google OAuth 2.0. When authorized, Asfysh receives temporary access tokens and refresh tokens issued by Google.

Local / Self-Hosted Use: Tokens and credentials are stored strictly in your local configuration files (e.g., your local Rclone configuration path or local environment variables) and are never transmitted to our servers.

Managed / Web Service Use (if applicable): If you use a hosted Asfysh relay/portal, tokens are encrypted at rest using industry-standard cryptography (AES-256) and used solely to execute user-instructed operations against the Google Drive API.

B. User Files and Content
Asfysh does not inspect, read, copy, sell, or retain your files. All data payloads (documents, media, archives, and binaries) transfer directly between your local client machine and Google Drive?s storage endpoints. Asfysh only processes file metadata (such as filenames, MIME types, and file IDs) in-memory as required to fulfill standard file-system operations (listing directories, reading sizes, confirming checksums).

C. Operational & Diagnostic Data
When visiting our website or utilizing hosted services, we may collect basic server logs containing:

IP address, browser user-agent, and operating system

Timestamps of API adapter calls

Diagnostic error codes (e.g., HTTP 429 rate limit events)

2. How We Use Information
We use the information processed strictly to:

Authenticate your Google Drive session with Rclone.

Execute storage and directory commands commanded by you (e.g., sync, copy, mount, ls).

Prevent abuse, mitigate rate limits, and maintain service stability.

Respond to customer inquiries or bug reports.

We do not sell, rent, monetize, or use your data for advertising, marketing profiling, or AI/ML model training.

3. Google API Services User Data Policy Compliance
Asfysh's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.

Specifically:

We only request the minimum OAuth scopes necessary to fulfill Rclone adapter functionality (such as [https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive](https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive) or [https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file](https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file)).

Human personnel cannot read your Google Drive data unless you explicitly provide diagnostic snippets to resolve a technical support issue.

Data obtained via Google APIs is never shared with third parties for targeted advertising or data broker exchanges.

4. Data Retention and Account Revocation
Revoking Access: You can revoke Asfysh?s access to your Google Account at any time through your Google Account Permissions.

Local Deletion: Deleting your local configuration file or application credentials immediately deletes any cached authentication tokens on your system.

5. Security Practices
We employ standard security protocols to safeguard all interactions with Asfysh:

All communication uses Transport Layer Security (TLS 1.3/1.2) encryption in transit.

In-memory processing architecture ensures file contents do not hit persistent disks on any intermediate relays.

Authentication credentials are never committed to public repositories or exposed in cleartext logs.

